{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.PtolemyTwist","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.PtolemyTwist","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Equiv","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.negTwist_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.negTwist_twist","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L280-L282","doc":"`negTwist` really negates, at every term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.sampleEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.sampleEq","kind":"def","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L262-L271","doc":"snappy's `- c_1002_1 * u^2 - c_1011_1 + c_1101_1 * u^2`, one of the 11 `u`-bearing\nequations among L6a4 class 1's 33, transcribed as a `TwistedEq`: signs `(-1,-1,+1)`,\ncocycle exponents `(2,0,2)`, each monomial a single coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.L6a4Coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.L6a4Coord","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L259-L260","doc":"The three Ptolemy coordinates appearing in the measured equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.sigmaFixed_isSolution_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.sigmaFixed_isSolution_neg","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L236-L249","doc":"**A `σ`-fixed point lies in both varieties.**  If every Ptolemy coordinate of `x` is\nfixed by `σ`, then `x` solves `P^c` and `P^{−c}` simultaneously.\n\n⚠ Read the file header before using this as the Sym² gate.  It says what follows *if* a\nself-dual representation gives a `σ`-fixed Ptolemy point; that identification is **not**\nestablished in this corpus.  The gate as actually argued runs through the obstruction\n*class* (`ObstructionH2.cls_eq_zero_of_cohomologous_neg`), not through this lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.eval_negTwist_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.eval_negTwist_one","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L223-L234","doc":"**The trivial cocycle is its own negative.**  At `u = 1` — the trivial obstruction\nclass — the twisted and negatively-twisted systems are literally the same equations, so\ntransport is the identity and no `σ` is needed.\n\nThis is the Lean counterpart of the one fixed point of `c ↦ -c` measured in\n`computations/ptolemy/obstruction_gerbe_involution.py`: `H²(M, ∂M; ℤ/3) ≅ (ℤ/3)³` has\norder 27 and exactly one element with `c = -c`, the trivial one.  It is also why the\nargument concludes what it does — the *only* class a self-dual representation could\ncarry is the one this lemma is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.exists_isSolution_negSystem_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.exists_isSolution_negSystem_iff","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L205-L221","doc":"**Non-emptiness is invariant.**  `P^c` has an `R`-point iff `P^{−c}` does.\n\nThis is what retires the compute question for the Sym² gate: whatever is true of one\ntwist is true of its negative, so the thirteen nontrivial L6a4 classes cannot be\nseparated from each other by emptiness alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.isSolution_negSystem_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.isSolution_negSystem_iff","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L192-L203","doc":"**Transport is reversible** for an injective `σ`: a point of `P^c` and its image in\n`P^{−c}` determine each other, so neither variety is \"more empty\" than the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.symm_apply_eq_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.symm_apply_eq_sq","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L184-L190","doc":"`σ` inverts `u`, hence so does `σ⁻¹`: from `σ u = u²` and `u³ = 1`, `σ (u²) = u⁴ = u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.isSolution_negSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.isSolution_negSystem","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L177-L182","doc":"**Transport.**  `σ` carries a solution of `P^c` to a solution of `P^{−c}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.negSystem_negSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.negSystem_negSystem","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L172-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.negSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.negSystem","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L168-L169","doc":"The system with the obstruction cocycle negated — snappy's `P^{−c}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.IsSolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.IsSolution","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L164-L166","doc":"A point `x` solves the system `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.eval_negTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.eval_negTwist","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L144-L156","doc":"**The relative step.**  Applying a ring endomorphism that inverts the cube root of\nunity to a point of the `c`-twisted equation evaluates the `(−c)`-twisted equation.\n\nThis is the Lean form of the measured statement *\"substituting `u ↦ u²` throughout `P^c`\nreproduces `P^{−c}` exactly as polynomial sets\"* — with the substitution acting on the\npoint rather than on the coefficients, which is the same map read on the other side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.negTwist_negTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.negTwist_negTwist","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L140-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.negTwist_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.negTwist_card","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.negTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.negTwist","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L132-L134","doc":"The same equation with the obstruction cocycle negated: `c ↦ -c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.eval","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L128-L130","doc":"Evaluate the equation at a point `x : V → R` with cube root of unity `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.mono","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L122-L122","doc":"the monomial of each term, as exponents on the Ptolemy coordinates ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.twist","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L120-L120","doc":"the exponent of `u` on each term — the obstruction cocycle ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.sign","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L118-L118","doc":"the integer coefficient of each term (in practice `±1`) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.card","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L116-L116","doc":"number of terms ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq.mk","kind":"ctor","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.TwistedEq","kind":"structure","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L107-L122","doc":"One equation of a Ptolemy variety carrying a `μ₃`-twist: a signed sum of monomials\nin the Ptolemy coordinates `V`, each term weighted by a power of the primitive cube root\nof unity.  The `twist` field **is** the obstruction cocycle's contribution.\n\nThis is a *description of the shape* snappy's equations were measured to have — see the\nfile header.  Nothing here claims that description is complete or canonical; it is the\nhypothesis under which the transport theorem below applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.map_zpow3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.map_zpow3","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L97-L103","doc":"A ring endomorphism sending `u` to `u²` sends `u^k` to `u^{-k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_neg","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L78-L95","doc":"**Negating the exponent is squaring.**  Over `μ₃`, `u^{-k} = u^{2k} = (u^k)²`.\nThis is the arithmetic content of the measured substitution `u ↦ u²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_base_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_base_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L75-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_one","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L72-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L69-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Ptolemy.zpow3","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/PtolemyTwist.lean#L65-L67","doc":"`u ^ k` for an exponent `k : ZMod 3`, via the canonical representative in `{0,1,2}`.\nWell-behaved exactly when `u ^ 3 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}